  "rationale": "Pareto target: quality (epsilon 0.03). summary_quality=0.887 is the only judge with gradient; schema_adherence and output_json_valid are already 1.0. Round 1's critique established that this judge primarily scores the `summary` field, so edits to section_summary.md are the direct lever. Current skill lists what to preserve but gives no scorable shape; models default to generic 'This section discusses...' phrasing that loses points for faithfulness. The added skeleton (<obligated party> <operative verb from source> <obligation>[, exception]) maps 1:1 to how FINRA/legal summaries are graded for completeness and faithfulness: it forces the model to name the regulated party (firm/member/associated person), lock the operative modal verb verbatim (must/shall/may/is prohibited from \u2014 a known failure mode when models paraphrase 'shall' as 'should'), and attach exceptions/carve-outs explicitly. Tightening the cap from 1-3 to 1-2 sentences stays inside output_schema.md's '1-3' bound (no clash) and gives a small secondary latency benefit by shortening long summaries. No clash with hierarchy/citations/exclusions/output_schema (none constrain summary wording). No prior reverted mutation on this file. Predicted summary_quality 0.887 \u2192 0.94-0.97 \u2192 aggregate 0.97+, clearing the +0.03 epsilon; worst case is a small lift within noise and we still clear the \u22120.03 regression band.",
